+# N12 synthetic prediction and model evidence contract
+
+2026-11-04. One owner-approved mission under the exact preexisting DE-N12-SYNTHETIC-01. Official requirements R09/R24/R39/R56; ten acceptance groups A–J in the retained preflight matrix. All original scientific/source/prerequisite/hardware/release gates remain. No operational promotion, N16 execution, private cognition, Qwen or acquisition.
+
+## Frozen engineering experiment, before first execution
+
+Only heart_rate (/min) and hrv (ms), horizons 5/15/30/60 minutes, persistence, ordinary least squares and Theil–Sen trends. Thirty-minute input window at 60-second cadence (31 points), all good/confidence>=0.7/no artifact, full source and knowledge eligibility, maximum age90s. Missing/gapped/stale or current absolute personal deviation>2 sample standard deviations abstains. Two SD is an authored demonstration eligibility band, not a clinical threshold. Raw and same-person sample-SD deviations are both preserved. Prior reference720 hourly authored values per crew/metric; no cross-person ranking.
+
+Unchanged N09 generator supplies dated fictional measurements. Main train: crew01/02, nominal/post-exercise, anchor−5days. Calibration: crew03/04, radiation-spike/communication-blackout, anchor−4days. Test: crew05/06, cardiorespiratory-drift/controlled-hr-rise/sensor-dropout/contradictory-sensors/sleep-fatigue, anchor−3days. Separate seen nominal robustness: all six crew at anchor−2days. Separate analytical arithmetic controls: all six crew at anchor−1day; HR z=0.1+0.012*elapsed_minutes, HRV z=−0.006*elapsed_minutes. These transformations are authored tests, not physiology. Each of30 units contains181 minute frames. Labels and future target frames are evaluation-only. Mechanical main crew/scenario/time separation does not establish scientific independence; personal prior references are available for every fictional crew.
+
